UID:b468985a155e83b1@role-employment-labor.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261001T223937Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Gov. Mills Proclaims October 2026 as Disabili
 ty Employment Awareness Month
DESCRIPTION:Skip First Level Navigation\nSkip All Navigation\nMaine.gov\nA
 gencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Maine.gov\nMaine Departmen
 t of Labor\nContact Us\n|\nNews\n|\nOnline services\n|\nPublications\n|\nS
 itemap\nHome\nContact Us\nOnline Services\nAbout MDOL\nNews & Events\nForm
 s & Publications\nMDOL Bureaus\nHome\n→\nNews & Events\n→ Gov. Mills P
 roclaims October 2026 as Disability Employment Awareness Month\nServices\n
 Jobs & Training\nUnemployment Insurance\nDisability Services\nWorkplace Sa
 fety\nLabor Laws\nLabor Statistics\nWorkforce Development\nGov. Mills Proc
 laims October 2026 as Disability Employment Awareness Month\nOctober 1\, 2
 026\nFor Immediate Release: Oct. 1\, 2026\nMedia Contact: Autumn Mahoney\,
  Communications Specialist\nmedia.dol@maine.gov\nAUGUSTA\n- Gov. Janet T. 
 Mills has proclaimed October 2026 as\nNational Disability Employment Aware
 ness Month\n(NDEAM).\nOctober 2026 marks the 81st anniversary of NDEAM. Go
 v. Mills' proclamation recognizes the contributions of people with disabil
 ities to Maine's workplaces\, communities and economy and calls on employe
 rs\, schools\, higher education institutions and community organizations t
 o promote access to good\, in-demand jobs and career pathways\, including 
 registered apprenticeship.\n"At a time when employers are searching for wo
 rkers\, talented Maine people with disabilities are ready and willing to p
 articipate in the workforce\," said Jennifer Kimble\, the chair of Maine's
  Commission on Disability and Employment. "Expanding recruitment and reten
 tion strategies that recognize the value of including workers with disabil
 ities as benefits businesses\, communities\, and the individuals whose tal
 ents are too often underutilized."\nThe Commission on Disability and Emplo
 yment was established by the legislature in 1997 and promotes collaboratio
 n with the public and private sectors to increase awareness and influence 
 policy related to employment for people with disabilities. Its members env
 ision a Maine workforce that includes all people with disabilities employe
 d in jo\nhttp://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=13363746
URL:http://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=13363746
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:23490cc63b7ca666@role-employment-labor.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261001T223937Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] October Is National Disability Employment Awa
 reness Month
DESCRIPTION:Skip First Level Navigation\nSkip All Navigation\nMaine.gov\nA
 gencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Maine.gov\nMaine Departmen
 t of Labor\nContact Us\n|\nNews\n|\nOnline services\n|\nPublications\n|\nS
 itemap\nHome\nContact Us\nOnline Services\nAbout MDOL\nNews & Events\nForm
 s & Publications\nMDOL Bureaus\nHome\n→\nNews & Events\n→ October Is N
 ational Disability Employment Awareness Month\nServices\nJobs & Training\n
 Unemployment Insurance\nDisability Services\nWorkplace Safety\nLabor Laws\
 nLabor Statistics\nWorkforce Development\nOctober Is National Disability E
 mployment Awareness Month\nOctober 1\, 2026\nGov. Janet T. Mills has procl
 aimed October 2026 as\nNational Disability Employment Awareness Month\n(ND
 EAM)\n.\nMaine is an Employment First state\, affirming employment as the 
 first and preferred option for people with disabilities who receive servic
 es from state agencies. The governor's proclamation calls on employers\, s
 chools\, higher education institutions and community organizations to prom
 ote access to good\, in-demand jobs and career pathways\, including regist
 ered apprenticeship.\nGet involved this October!\nThis year marks the 81st
  anniversary of NDEAM\, and organizations across Maine and nationally are 
 offering events\, trainings and other activities throughout the month. Whe
 ther you're an employer interested in inclusive hiring\, a jobseeker explo
 ring career opportunities\, a workforce professional\, a student\, a famil
 y member or a community partner\, there are ways to participate.\nWe encou
 rage you to browse the events and activities below.\nThank you for helping
  celebrate the contributions of people with disabilities and promote acces
 s to meaningful employment and career opportunities across Maine.\nTo help
  promote awareness\, printable MDOL NDEAM posters are also\ndownloadable h
 ere\n. For more information about employment services for people with disa
 bilities\, visit the Maine Department of Labor's\nBureau of Rehabilitation
  Services\n.\nOctober NDEAM-related events and activities\nFor employers a
 nd workforce de\nhttp://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=1
 3363743
URL:http://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=13363743
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
